  <content>
  <section id="sect-00001"><title>Activity</title>
<para id="para-00001">The function \(B\) is defined by the equation \(B(x) = 10x + 25\). Use the graphing tool here or technology outside the course. Graph the function.</para>
<media alt=""><iframe src="../../media/desmos/a47b5bb4ba783be55a7067b919f165f14dcc36ce.html" width="500" height="400"/></media>
<para id="para-00002">If needed, remember -</para>
<list id="list-00001">
  <item>You can collapse the equation entry tab by selecting the button.</item>
  <item>To change the scale along either the x- or \(y\)-axis, click on the wrench button and then enter minimum and maximum values for each axis and set the step value.</item>
  <item>To find a point on the line, click on the line and drag the mouse along the line to display the ordered pairs for each location.</item>
</list>

<!--Question 1 -->
<exercise id="exer-00001">
  <problem id="prob-00001">
    <para id="para-00003">What is the value of \(B(6)\)?</para>
    </problem><solution id="sol-00001">
    
    
  
  <para id="para-00004">Compare your answer:</para>
    
    <para id="para-00005">\(B(6) = 85\)</para>
  
  </solution></exercise>

<!--Question 2 -->
<exercise id="exer-00002">
  <problem id="prob-00002">
    <para id="para-00006">What were the window values you used for the \(x\)-axis? (Write the values as an inequality.)</para>
    </problem><solution id="sol-00002">
    
    
  
  <para id="para-00007">Compare your answer:</para>
    
    <para id="para-00008">\(-1 \leq x \leq 7\)</para>
  
  </solution></exercise>

<!--Question 3 -->
<exercise id="exer-00003">
  <problem id="prob-00003">
    <para id="para-00009">What were the window values you used for the \(y\)-axis? (Write the values as an inequality.)</para>
    </problem><solution id="sol-00003">
    
    
  
  <para id="para-00010">Compare your answer:</para>
    
    <para id="para-00011">\(-1 \leq y \leq 100\)</para>
  
  </solution></exercise>

<!--Question 4 -->
<exercise id="exer-00004">
  <problem id="prob-00004">
    <para id="para-00012">What is the value of \(B(2.75)\)?</para>
    </problem><solution id="sol-00004">
    
    
  
  <para id="para-00013">Compare your answer:</para>
    
    <para id="para-00014">\(B(2.75) = 52.5\)</para>
  
  </solution></exercise>

<!--Question 5 -->
<exercise id="exer-00005">
  <problem id="prob-00005">
    <para id="para-00015">What is the value of \(B(1.482)\)?</para>
